 "last_activity": "2017-12-13T19:42:17Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "ML42mOuOAAAJ",
   "from": "Meghna Krishnadas",
   "author": "e092355034cc4723",
   "date": "2017-12-13T18:39:02Z",
   "subject": "specify measurement error for non-linear model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I am analyzing a non-linear relationship where the predictor variable has some measurement error. I have specified the model as:<br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:11pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">form = Y ~ a + b * me(logX, <a href=\"http://log.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://log.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640925000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3qenjGxfgY3wh-jJo6B5Gq\">log.sd</a>)\n</span></pre><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:11pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">priors &lt;- c(set_prior(&quot;normal(0,1)&quot;, nlpar = &quot;a&quot;),\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">            set_prior(&quot;normal(0,1)&quot;, nlpar = &quot;b&quot;))\n</span></pre><br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:11pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">nl2 &lt;- brm(bf(formula = form, \n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">             b ~ 1 + (1|G1), a ~ (1|G2), nl=T),\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           data = newdat2, prior = priors,\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           family = negbinomial(link=&quot;log&quot;), \n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           iter = 1000, chains = 4, cores = 4,\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           control = list(adapt_delta = 0.9),\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           save_model = &quot;brm-mod-NB-ME-nl.txt&quot;)</span></pre><br>This model does not compile - when I run the brm() call, it just moves to the cursor at the next line. <br><br>I&#39;m not sure why this is happening. Is it not possible to specify measurement error in non-linear models in brms? Any help will be much appreciated. <br><br>Thanks,<br>Meghna<br><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "neQqR1-SAAAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2017-12-13T19:42:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] specify measurement error for non-linear model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It is possible, but you cannot specify me() in the non-linear formula itself, since this formula is literally translated into stan code and me(...) doesn&#39;t make sense to Stan.<br><br></div>Instead, you can merge &quot;me()&quot; into b, which results in:<br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:11pt;outline:medium none currentcolor;border-color:currentcolor;border-style:none;border-width:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">bf(formula = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">Y ~ a + b</span>, \r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">   </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">b ~ 0 + </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">me(logX, <a href=\"http://log.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://log.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33i-9WO0UuasYImWK50jde\">log.sd</a>)</span></span> + (0 + </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">me(logX, <a href=\"http://log.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://log.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33i-9WO0UuasYImWK50jde\">log.sd</a>)</span></span> | G1), a ~ (1|G2), nl=T)<br></span></pre><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">In your special case, you might even further simplify your model to not using non-linear syntax at all:</div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:11pt;outline:medium none currentcolor;border-color:currentcolor;border-style:none;border-width:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">formula = </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">Y ~ </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">me(logX, <a href=\"http://log.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://log.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33i-9WO0UuasYImWK50jde\">log.sd</a>)</span></span> + (me</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">(logX, <a href=\"http://log.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://log.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33i-9WO0UuasYImWK50jde\">log.sd</a>)</span></span> | G1)</span></pre></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2017-12-13 19:39 GMT+01:00 Meghna Krishnadas <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">srishti...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I am analyzing a non-linear relationship where the predictor variable has some measurement error. I have specified the model as:<br><br><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:11pt;outline:medium none currentcolor;border-color:currentcolor;border-style:none;border-width:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">form = Y ~ a + b * me(logX, <a href=\"http://log.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://log.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33i-9WO0UuasYImWK50jde\">log.sd</a>)\r\n</span></pre><br><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:11pt;outline:medium none currentcolor;border-color:currentcolor;border-style:none;border-width:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">priors &lt;- c(set_prior(&quot;normal(0,1)&quot;, nlpar = &quot;a&quot;),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">            set_prior(&quot;normal(0,1)&quot;, nlpar = &quot;b&quot;))\r\n</span></pre><br><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:11pt;outline:medium none currentcolor;border-color:currentcolor;border-style:none;border-width:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:17px;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(50,50,50)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">nl2 &lt;- brm(bf(formula = form, \r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">             b ~ 1 + (1|G1), a ~ (1|G2), nl=T),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           data = newdat2, prior = priors,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           family = negbinomial(link=&quot;log&quot;), \r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           iter = 1000, chains = 4, cores = 4,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           control = list(adapt_delta = 0.9),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51);white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,120,51)\">           save_model = &quot;brm-mod-NB-ME-nl.txt&quot;)</span></pre><br>This model does not compile - when I run the brm() call, it just moves to the cursor at the next line. <br><br>I&#39;m not sure why this is happening. Is it not possible to specify measurement error in non-linear models in brms? Any help will be much appreciated. <br><br>Thanks,<br>Meghna<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br><br></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;brms-users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brms-users+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brms-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/92b36428-97b9-43cd-81dc-90587403b01d%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/92b36428-97b9-43cd-81dc-90587403b01d%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2cMQ2yC_bB7yWqTA-Aij1z\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/92b36428-97b9-43cd-81dc-90587403b01d%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451640929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0MKbHh3mWe1Iev5mvkAD77\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div></div>\r\n"
